{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux’s plugin system is a single protocol ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":") with four lifecycle hooks and an ordered registry ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost"},{"type":"text","text":"). All store extensibility flows through this contract. The built-in "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" use it, and so do domain-specific features like killswitch enforcement and paywall management."}]},{"anchor":"The-Dispatch-Lifecycle","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The Dispatch Lifecycle"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every call to "},{"code":"store.send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" drives plugins through a four-phase lifecycle:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["plugins.willReduce(state:action:)      \/\/ 1. Pre-reduce (read-only state)","appReducer.reduce(state:action:...)    \/\/ 2. App reducer runs","pluginEffects = plugins.reduce(...)    \/\/ 3. Plugin reducers run","plugins.afterReduce(state:action:)     \/\/ 4. Post-reduce cleanup"],"syntax":null},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The generic "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store"},{"type":"text","text":" implements this lifecycle internally. You don’t write "},{"code":"send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" by hand — "},{"code":"Store.send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" handles packing, reducing, plugin hooks, unpacking, and effect dispatch."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A fifth method, "},{"code":"flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", runs once at shutdown to drain async buffers."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All four hooks have default no-op implementations. Each plugin overrides only what it needs."}]},{"anchor":"Core-Middleware-vs-Domain-Plugins","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Core Middleware vs Domain Plugins"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin system serves two structurally different roles. Recognizing which one a plugin fills determines where it lives, which hooks it uses, and how it couples to the host app."}]},{"anchor":"Core-Middleware","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Core Middleware"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" are "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"action-agnostic infrastructure","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":". They never inspect the "},{"code":"Action","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" type, never dispatch actions, and never return effects. They couple only to the shape of state:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" needs keypaths to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" properties.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" needs ","type":"text"},{"code":"State: Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" so it can snapshot and compare.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because they don’t touch actions, they work with any app that uses Swidux — no wiring required beyond construction."}]},{"anchor":"Domain-Plugins","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Domain Plugins"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Killswitch, parental gate, and paywall plugins are "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"domain-specific modules","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" that ship as separate library targets ("},{"code":"SwiduxKillswitch","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"SwiduxParentalGate","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). They own their own state slices and action enums, dispatch effects, and must be explicitly wired into the host app’s root types."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each domain plugin stores three wiring pieces:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["private let stateKeyPath: WritableKeyPath<RootState, FeatureState>","private let toRootAction: @Sendable (FeatureAction) -> RootAction","private let extractAction: @Sendable (RootAction) -> FeatureAction?"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The host app provides these at init — the plugin never assumes a specific root type."}]},{"anchor":"Importing-at-call-sites","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Importing at call sites"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because each domain plugin ships as a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"separate library target","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", its state and action types are defined in that module — not in "},{"code":"Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A common convention is to re-export core Swidux from "},{"code":"AppState.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"code":"@_exported import Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", but that re-exports "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"core Swidux only","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":"; it does not re-export the plugin modules."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"So any file that reads a plugin-owned slice ("},{"code":"store.analytics.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"store.paywall.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"store.killswitch.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", …) or dispatches a plugin action ("},{"code":"AnalyticsAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"PaywallAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", …) must import that plugin’s module in "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"that","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" file:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"touches ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.analytics.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" → ","type":"text"},{"code":"import SwiduxAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"touches ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.paywall.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" → ","type":"text"},{"code":"import SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"touches only ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.ui","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":".ui(...)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (app-module types) → nothing extra","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The easy case to forget is a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"View","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" that reads the slice for display — "},{"code":"AppState.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"AppAction.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" already import the module, but the View is a different file. Without the import you get:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["property 'isOptedOut' is not available due to missing import of defining module 'SwiduxAnalytics'","property 'isPro' is not available due to missing import of defining module 'SwiduxPaywall'"],"syntax":null},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is to add "},{"code":"import Swidux<Plugin>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to that file."}]},{"anchor":"Comparison","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Comparison"},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Core Middleware","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Domain Plugins","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Action knowledge","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"None","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Full — extracts and lifts actions","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Lifecycle hooks","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"text":" only","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Returns effects","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"No","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Yes","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"State coupling","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keypath to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"text":" constraint","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keypath to plugin’s own state slice","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Wiring","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Construction only","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keypath + action lifter + action extractor","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Target","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Core ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"text":" library","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Separate library target","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Opt-in","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Instantiate and register","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add state, action case, and register","type":"text"}]}]]]},{"anchor":"The-Decision-Rule","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The Decision Rule"},{"type":"aside","style":"important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Does the middleware need to know your action type? If ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"no","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", it’s core middleware — put it in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"text":" and use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"text":". If ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"yes","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", it’s a domain plugin — give it its own target and use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Important"},{"anchor":"Hook-Selection-Guide","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Hook Selection Guide"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce(state:action:)"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Capture state ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the reducer mutates it. State is read-only. Use for snapshots (undo) or pre-mutation analytics.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce(state:action:) -> Effect?"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Handle domain-specific actions ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"after"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the app reducer. Mutate the plugin’s state slice and return effects. This is the only hook that can dispatch actions or do async work.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce(state:action:)"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Observe state ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"after"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" all reducing is done. Use for persistence draining, logging, or metrics. Cannot return effects.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush() async"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Shutdown hook. Flush pending async buffers (persistence writes, analytics batches). Called once when the app exits.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Registration-Order","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Registration Order"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost"},{"type":"text","text":" executes plugins in registration order. Recommended ordering:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. Must snapshot before any mutation","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. Drains changelogs after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. Domain plugins in any order","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Undo must come first — it snapshots state in "},{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", before the app reducer or any plugin modifies it. Persistence typically comes next so its "},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" drain sees the final state. Domain plugins use only "},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so their relative order rarely matters."}]},{"anchor":"Service-Result-Actions-and-Transition-Observation","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Service-Result Actions and Transition Observation"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"service-result action","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"code":"PaywallPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"code":"customerInfoUpdated","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"KillswitchPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"code":"verdictReceived","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureFlagsPlugin"},{"text":"’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"refreshSucceeded","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — fires on ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"every"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" fetch, refresh, or stream tick, not","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only when the value changed, and unconditionally writes its payload to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state slice. The payload is frequently identical to what is already there"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(a re-delivered entitlement, an unchanged remote config)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Do "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"not","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" map analytics or side effects to the raw service-result action:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"it fires duplicates by design. Observe the ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"state slice","type":"text"}]},{"text":" — or a value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"derived from it — instead.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"State observation is already deduplicated by the framework. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.send"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"packs the observer into a value-type snapshot, lets reducers mutate the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"snapshot, then writes back via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State.apply"},{"text":". For a leaf slice that write","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"is a plain assignment whose ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"text":" setter equality-gates ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"values, so a slice whose value did not change emits no notification — and a","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"value-diffing consumer such as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsIdentity.userProperties"},{"type":"text","text":" (which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" re-evaluates and diffs every non-analytics dispatch) sees exactly the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"real transitions. This dedup is a property of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":", not of any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per-plugin guard, so a no-op service-result cycle is silent to state"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"observers without any extra reducer logic.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Next-Steps","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Next Steps"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" — Step-by-step guide to creating a domain plugin","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — Configure the built-in persistence middleware"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo"},{"type":"text","text":" — Add undo\/redo with the built-in undo middleware"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"title":"Plugin Architecture"},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Explanation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture"],"generated":true,"title":"Explanation"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"article","references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingADomainPlugin":{"title":"Building a Domain Plugin","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Create a self-contained feature plugin with its own state, actions, and effects.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingadomainplugin","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginHost":{"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PluginHost","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PluginHost","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginhost","title":"PluginHost","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Ordered registry of plugins that drives the dispatch lifecycle."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxPlugin":{"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxplugin","abstract":[{"text":"A plugin that participates in the Swidux dispatch cycle.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"SwiduxPlugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ArchitectureGuide":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system."}],"kind":"article","title":"Architecture & Performance"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/DesignPrinciples":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples","title":"Design Principles","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them."}],"kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"UndoPlugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoRedo":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoredo","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"article","title":"Undo \/ Redo"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"title":"Swidux","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","role":"collection"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistencemiddlewareguide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure automatic persistence that drains entity changes and batches database writes."}],"kind":"article","title":"Persistence Middleware"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every mutation for downstream persistence."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"EntityStore"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SecurityPosture":{"role":"collectionGroup","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/securityposture","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What Swidux’s soft controls actually guarantee, and what to do when you need a hard one."}],"kind":"article","title":"Security Posture"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Store"}],"title":"Store","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Store"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Generic store that owns the dispatch cycle, plugin lifecycle, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"observation layer.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistencePlugin"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistencePlugin"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Coalescing persistence plugin."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"PersistencePlugin"}}}